<p>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>
<center>
<table align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="80%">
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>B</b>&nbsp;</font>eing a social lot, we are happy to consider new players for membership in the Armigers of Mirth.	
		For the benefit of all concerned, we do however have a few requirements.		
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>		
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>A</b>&nbsp;</font>pplicants must read, understand, and agree to abide by the rules and behavior as explained in our 
		<a class="BaseC" href="Guildcharter.asp" target="_self"><b>charter</b></a>. The rules are not negotiable and repeated failure to abide by them may result in removal from The 
		Guild.
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2r.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>W</b>&nbsp;</font>hile we do not require roleplaying at all times, we believe that role playing adds flavor to the game and
		certainly suggest role playing as much as possible.	In light of this, applicants must have a name the reflects positively on The Guild 
		and therefor doesn't mock Dark Age of Camelot©, imply vulgarity, plagarize, steal proper names, or resemble something other than a reasonable sounding
		fantasy name. For example, StudMan, KoolDewd, TygerWoodz, Skrewu, etc. would all be unacceptable.
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>S</b>&nbsp;</font>ince we hope to bring in members that fit well into our Guild we require a &quot;getting-to-know-you&quot; period before
		membership. This entails the applicant grouping and playing with other Armigers on no less than 3 different
		occassions. Additionally during that time you must have played with at least 4 different Guild members. The purpose of this is
		to determine if our Guild and style of play is a good match for the applicant. 
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>	
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2r.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>A</b>&nbsp;</font>fter having played with Armiger members for the prescribed time, the players who have grouped with the 
		applicant will take a vote on membership. The acceptance vote must reach a consensus, any 'nays' and the applicant's
		request for membership will be refused. Acceptance requires a good toast and several rounds of drinks - to be supplied by
		the new member of course!
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>
		
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB"><font size="3" class="MainBReverse">&nbsp;<b>M</b>&nbsp;</font>embers may be promoted to Guild Officers if they have shown good judgement, fair play, and are living by the
		goals of The Guild. Promotion requires a consensus vote by all current Guild Officers. Promotion requires many a' good toast and a 
		drinking party afterwards!
		</font>
		</td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB" align="center"><img src="images/arm_spear2r.gif" WIDTH="497" HEIGHT="21"></td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">If you think you'd be interesting in joining the Armigers, please look for any of our <a class="BaseC" href="CharactersView.asp" target="_self"><b>characters</b></a> online - or you may reach some of our officers via email; 
			<a class="BaseC" href="mailto:kalls001@umn.edu"><b>Baronlinc</b></a> or  
			<a class="BaseC" href="mailto:morpeth@armigersofmirth.com"><b>Morpeth</b></a>.
		</td>
	</tr>

</table>	
	
</body>
</html>
